  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "An iterative agent, not a fixed pipeline",
      "items": [
        "The LLM chooses tools using always-loaded warehouse rules and warehouse-analysis / charts skills. Discover, query, inspect and verify can repeat.",
        "describe_data merges dbt manifest/catalog, Cube metadata and access-filtered ClickHouse system tables. Missing sources yield explicit notices; the cache can be refreshed."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Two separate access controls",
      "items": [
        "With authentication enabled, only configured user IDs/emails pass the allowlist. Single-user mode is allowed. Queries cover all users; no per-user row scoping.",
        "run_sql checks one read statement and adds a display limit where needed. ClickHouse grants and constrained limits enforce access; errors return hints to the model."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Chart execution and persistence",
      "items": [
        "Normal create_chart(sql=...) runs the SQL again, validates rows/mapping, builds an envelope and writes /charts/<thread>/<slug>.plotly.json. Failures return errors for revision.",
        "A custom figure uses run_sql(save_as=...), thread scratch and execute under the shared approval policy. When enabled, non-allowlisted commands pause; only approved execution proceeds.",
        "The frontend reads the stored envelope through /files/read. Tool results in message history restore the card on reopening; Plotly renders charts, native components render tables/KPIs."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Example: failed runs by day",
      "items": [
        "Inspect fct_run \u2192 count/sample the date window \u2192 aggregate error/timeout by day \u2192 verify totals \u2192 create a bar chart \u2192 explain the comparison.",
        "Treat interrupted as an approval pause. If no chart is useful, return the verified number with its window and caveat."
      ]
    }
  ]
